# probe (quest rework P6): setting map.<NAME> <value>, an assignment to xi.settings.map[NAME] (before the login a header
# line, after it a step). Through The Gift (otherAreas 21), whose offer needs xi.settings.map.FISHING_ENABLE == true
# (false by default), Under the Sea completed and The Sand Charm accepted. Recorded on the Lua quest; the replay ran a
# test-only C# copy of its offer (on Settings.MapFlag), removed once The Gift shipped in Other Areas group 2. The Gift is
# now C#: the replay runs the port, a re-record is refused, and the probe stays as a C#-side regression check. Only the
# Lua table changes: the engine's own fishing stays off.
lists Selbina/Oswald/onTrigger Selbina/onEventFinish/70
char zone=Selbina pos=48.6,-15.273,7.989 job=WAR lvl=30
setting map.FISHING_ENABLE true         # header
quest OtherAreas.UnderTheSea completed
quest OtherAreas.TheSandCharm accepted
login
trigger Oswald                          # fishing on: the offer, 70 (DANCESHROOM)
finish option=0                         # not taken (50 takes it)
setting map.FISHING_ENABLE false        # a step
trigger Oswald                          # fishing off: no section, Oswald's own script
finish-if-event
setting map.FISHING_ENABLE true         # a step
trigger Oswald                          # 70 again
finish option=50                        # begun
